{
  "dom_id": "questionExplanation-256513",
  "name": null,
  "problem": "",
  "worked_solution": "The formula for the Newton-Raphson method is\n\n$$\n{x}_{n+1}={x}_{n}-\\frac{f({x}_{n})}{{f}^{′}({x}_{n})}\n$$\n\nwhere ${f}^{′}({x}_{n})$ is the derivative of $f(x)$ evaluated at ${x}_{n}.$\n\nIn our case, we have\n\n$$\n{f}^{′}(x)={(\\operatorname{cos}⁡x-\\frac{x-4}{5})}^{′}=-\\operatorname{sin}⁡x-\\frac{1}{5}\n$$\n\nTherefore, our Newton-Raphson formula is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{n+1} & ={x}_{n}-\\frac{\\operatorname{cos}⁡{x}_{n}-\\frac{{x}_{n}-4}{5}}{-\\operatorname{sin}⁡{x}_{n}-\\frac{1}{5}} \\\\  & ={x}_{n}+\\frac{5\\operatorname{cos}⁡{x}_{n}-{x}_{n}+4}{5\\operatorname{sin}⁡{x}_{n}+1}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nStarting with ${x}_{0}=4.8,$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} & ={x}_{0}+\\frac{5\\operatorname{cos}⁡{x}_{0}-{x}_{0}+4}{5\\operatorname{sin}⁡{x}_{0}+1} \\\\  & =4.8+\\frac{5\\operatorname{cos}⁡(4.8)-4.8+4}{5\\operatorname{sin}⁡(4.8)+1} \\\\  & ≈4.891,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nrounded to three decimal places.",
  "calculator_instructions": "",
  "fields": [],
  "problem_field_keys": [],
  "answer_fields_complete": null,
